(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["me-easy-2026-010"]={"v":1,"id":"me-easy-2026-010","title":"Mock Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","sourceTitle":"Mock Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","branch":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING","code":"ME","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering","seriesId":"me-easy-2026","num":10,"category":"mock","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering"},"source":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Mechanical_Engineering/019_Mock Level Test-1 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The given question is followed by three statements labelled I, II and III. You have to study the question and all the three statements given to decide whether any information provide in the statement(s) is/are redundant and can be dispensed with while answering the given question.<br />\nWhat is the average salary of 15 employees?<br />\n1. Average salary of 7 clerical cadre (out of the 15 employees) is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/a8/a81a9ced9a559c1fedd1.png\" /><br />\n2. Average salary of 5 officer cadre (out of the 15 employees) is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/542474f1352b890dc68d.png\" /><br />\n3. Average salary of the 3 sub-staff employees (out of the 15 employees) is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8ef1171dea637257a1dc.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7b/7b88d932d88ee84e01e4.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Find the wrong number in the series:<br />\n7, 28, 63, 124, 215, 342</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"7"},{"key":"B","html":"28"},{"key":"C","html":"124"},{"key":"D","html":"215"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/348dd4a978ce644b4599.png\" /></div>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A square field ABCD of side 90 m is so located that its diagonal AC is from north to south and the corner B is to the west of D. Rohan and Rahul start walking along the sides from B and C respectively in the clockwise and anti-clockwise directions with speeds of 8 km/hr and 10 km/hr. Where shall they cross each other the second time?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"On AD at a distnace of 30 m from A."},{"key":"B","html":"On BC at a distance of 10 m from B."},{"key":"C","html":"On AD at a distance of 30 m from D."},{"key":"D","html":"On BC at a distance of 10 m from C."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e9/e933e01cf1901775340c.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"18"},{"key":"D","html":"21"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/14/14e22c5fb7d36b1e2aa8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The sum of the first n terms in the sequence 7, 77, 777, 7777, .......... is _____.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8e9db928e3d46c6ab582.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/68/6896c04ddbd0dc215d09.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c9/c9773669bffb7ba5bd4c.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/33/3312653475d8b5a46df3.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b54db78fd36edddf688e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>We have two rectangular sheets of paper, M and N, each of dimensions 6 cm × 1 cm. Sheet M is rolled to form a (closed - ended) cylinder by bringing the long edges together. Sheet N is cut into equal square patches and assembled to form the largest possible closed cube. Assuming the ends of the cylinder are closed, the ratio (volume of cylinder): (Volume of cube) is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b7/b76799e079b73c4c064d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2c/2c8acf3aee7115c71d4b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cba5fc82284f27884639.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5306bb7e17c9d7bc827.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cb/cb3d662d6f4a80a0ed8a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":7,"type":"MSQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In the adjoining figure <em>D</em>, <em>E</em> and <em>F</em> are the mid-points of the sides <em>BC</em>, <em>AC</em> and <em>AB</em> respectively.<br />\nΔ<em>DEF</em> is congruent to triangle.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/52/524d84853626a368beaf.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"AFE"},{"key":"B","html":"ABC"},{"key":"C","html":"BFD"},{"key":"D","html":"CDE"}],"answer":["A","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/aa/aa1c49da3d1f3e62c2ef.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A group of six friends named Peter, Qadir, Roger, Shah, Tarun and Usman have different height<br />\nand weight. They are ranked such that the heaviest is ranked 1 and the tallest is ranked 1 in<br />\nrespective category. Some more details are known:<br />\n<strong>I.</strong> Peter is shorter but heavier than Shah<br />\n<strong>II.</strong> Roger and Tarun are heavier but shorter than Peter and Usman<br />\n<strong>III.</strong> Shah is heavier but shorter than Qadir but neither of them is either the tallest or the heaviest.<br />\nThe rank of Qadir, if all are arranged in descending order of their height and the tallest is given rank 1, is __________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e2699b69e546b9cf571.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2bd919fafa1eef1fb337.png\" /></div>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The question given below has a main statement followed by four choices. Choose the option which follows the main statement given below within the quotes.<br />\n“Whenever the demand for electricity rises, supply from GENCO increases.”</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The supply increases, it means demand has risen."},{"key":"B","html":"The demand has risen therefore the supply from GENCO increases."},{"key":"C","html":"The supply decreases implies the demand is low."},{"key":"D","html":"Both (b) and (c)"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f7/f7e88dfa13b24318adb9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Given below is a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way. Federer’s fifth grand slam win prompted a reporter to ask whether he was the best ever. Federer is certainly not lacking in confidence, but he wasn’t about to proclaim himself the best ever. “The best player of this generation, yes”, he said, “But nowhere close to ever. Just look at the records that some guys have. I’m a minnow.” _______________</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"His win against Agassi, a genius from the previous generation, contradicts that."},{"key":"B","html":"Sampras, the king of an earlier generation, was as humble."},{"key":"C","html":"He is more than a minnow to his contemporaries."},{"key":"D","html":"The difference between ‘the best of this generation’ and ‘the best ever’ is a matter of perception."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nOption &lsquo;c&rsquo; is the most appropriate way of completing the given paragraph.</p>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Flow through a horizontal pipe section of uniform diameter with side tappings is shown below</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c8bb4de93d32a5dfb2f0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Take friction factor as ‘f ’. The total frictional head loss in the pipe section is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d8239ba53cbc69fefb73.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/468ce23b41cd0683d703.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/96/96f40ab7ffe22db40401.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/94f85da5624d2e38ad17.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/92f0af1a353c41897962.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8d15dfd3a39264f9f373.png\" /></div>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A simply supported beam <em>AB</em> of span 8 m is loaded as shown in the figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/fae40befa7df3e9b7b93.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which portion of the beam is subjected to pure bending?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"AC"},{"key":"B","html":"CD"},{"key":"C","html":"DB"},{"key":"D","html":"None of the above"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b04518357fb03008a947.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A small car weighing 10000 N runs along a level unbanked road of mean radius 300 m. The inner and the outer wheels are 1 m apart. The centre of gravity of the car is 0.6 m above the road level. The coefficient of friction between the road surface and the tyres is 0.3 m. The lowest speed at<br />\nwhich the car will overturn is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"49.5 m/s"},{"key":"B","html":"29.7 m/s"},{"key":"C","html":"70 m/s"},{"key":"D","html":"35 m/s"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/83e9db77e9472371747b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Which of the following defects involves the formation of a cation vacancy along with a cationinterstitial pair?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Frenkel defect"},{"key":"B","html":"Schottky defect"},{"key":"C","html":"Selt-interstitial defect"},{"key":"D","html":"Substitutional defect"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\n<strong>Frenkel defect :</strong> It might be thought of as being formed by a cation leaving its normal position<br />\nand moving into an interstitial site. There is no change in charge as the cation maintains same<br />\npositive charge as an interstitial.</p>"},{"n":15,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A single point turning tool has an actual clearance angle of 7°. While turning a workpiece of diameter 80 mm diameter, the effective clearance angle reduces to 2.4°. Which of the following tool setting errors has occurred?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Tool is kept 1.7 mm above the workpiece center."},{"key":"B","html":"Tool is kept 3.2 mm below the workpiece center."},{"key":"C","html":"Tool is kept 3.2 mm above the workpiece center."},{"key":"D","html":"Tool is kept 6.4 mm above the workpiece center."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/87/87421c4b52dc4fd9a9a2.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d59710d6e2cee9f073a6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":16,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The number of instantaneous centre of rotation for the mechanism shown below is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/85/85af094eb463934c1113.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"6"},{"key":"B","html":"12"},{"key":"C","html":"30"},{"key":"D","html":"15"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/8359d20f0337485253b5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A centrifugal clutch, transmitting power at 600 rpm and consists of four shoes, each having a mass of 3 kg. The clutch just gets engaged at 300 rpm. The radius of the centre of gravity of each shoe is 120 mm, when engaged. The inner radius of the drum is 150 mm. The coefficient of friction between the shoe and the drum is 0.25. The power transmitted by the clutch is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"5 kW"},{"key":"B","html":"10 kW"},{"key":"C","html":"2.5 kW"},{"key":"D","html":"20 kW"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/379aaea67fcf6f343b94.png\" /></div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>An ideal reheat rankine cycle has an efficiency of 0.52. The work output from high and low pressure turbines are 832 kJ/kg and 1528 kJ/kg respectively. The work input to the pump is 17 kJ/kg. The enthalpy of saturated liquid and saturated vapour at condenser pressure are 198 kJ/kg<br />\nand 2547 kJ/kg respectively. The moisture content at the entry to the condenser is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"7.93%"},{"key":"B","html":"9.20%"},{"key":"C","html":"11.21%"},{"key":"D","html":"5.46%"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b3/b3d3ffe64aa07ce530ba.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A volume of 200 m<sup>3</sup> of air passes through a Psychrometric process. The condition of air at inlet is 40°C DBT, 30°C WBT with a specific enthalpy of 86.5 kJ/kg. The outlet condition of air is 35°DBT and 30° WBT. The specific enthalpy of air at the outlet is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"53.7 kJ/kg"},{"key":"B","html":"66.6 kJ/kg"},{"key":"C","html":"78.9 kJ/kg"},{"key":"D","html":"86.5 kJ/kg"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/92f0c04fea37207f1fca.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In an assembly line, the total work content is 400 seconds and the line is divided into 5 workstations.<br />\nThe station times (in seconds) are :</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4cf4ab308c026d94cb82.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Which of the following statements is correct?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The line efficiency is greater than 95%."},{"key":"B","html":"The line efficiency is less than 85% and the smoothness index is greater than 60s."},{"key":"C","html":"The balance delay is 20% and the line efficiency is 80%."},{"key":"D","html":"The smoothness index is 40s."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/dc/dc5a1ddcb484c193c72e.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5fe240c52d971d6cf12e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In an experiment, positive and negative values are equally likely to occur. The probability of obtaining at most one negative value in five trials is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2d/2dd8d66b87afd6c8c561.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/94c7118dffc9943f50d4.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d3/d301d166d533d4ded176.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e5/e505be096080469eaee3.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fe/feec98816e5382677823.png\" /></div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Let <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c9585f20762a1f2ea30.png\" /> If <em>I</em> is the 2 × 2 identity matrix and O is the 2 × 2 zero matrix, then</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2b405a62045fdb50b1ca.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/77ad3b272b8530552d7d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e2/e2f79a25885ad84723dc.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f5b779b58adbcaf43ff.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/06/06428ac8fd5d3b66a1a9.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/80efe26380a3fb69551c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The surface irregularities for a plane machined surface is shown below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e7/e7cccdab93e798575181.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The RMS value of surface roughness is ______ μm. [Correct upto three decimal places].</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.261,0.269],"answerText":"0.265","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.265 (0.261 - 0.269)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/16b5a1dae2548e412466.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A steel transmission shaft is subjected to fluctuating stresses. For calculating fatigue stress, the ASME fatigue failure criteria is used. If the ASME ellipse is drawn to a scale of 1 MPa = 1 mm, the length of the major axis of the ellipse (in mm) will be ______. [Rounded off to nearest integer] [Take, <em>s<sub>ut</sub></em> = 500 MPa, <em>s<sub>yt</sub></em> = 300 MPa, <em>s<sub>e</sub></em>′ = 150 MPa]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[600,600],"answerText":"600","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>600 (600 - 600)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a5/a50424f67023fab5f89b.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f34e306f18e2939d2f9a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":25,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A tube of uniform thickness has a section in the shape of a regular hexagon as shown in the figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/12/128a4d995f60a4d95073.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The tube rests in a horizontal position and is subjected to pure bending. If the bending stress at point <em>A</em> is 126 MPa, then the bending stress at point <em>B</em> will be ________ MPa. (Correct upto one decimal place)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[84,84],"answerText":"84.0","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>84.0 (84.0 - 84.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b05e89e353e38183284c.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d9f8cc9313cea1683ccf.png\" /></div>"},{"n":26,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A spherical ball of 5 cm in diameter is placed concentrically inside a large spherical furnace, such that 25% of the energy emitted by the furnace reaches the ball. The diameter of the spherical furnace is____ mm.<br />\n(Rounded off to the nearest integer)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[100,100],"answerText":"100","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>100 (100 - 100)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/547466334f562cba158c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The magnitude of the position vector of the centroid of the given area from origin O is _____ mm.<br />\n(Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3c/3ceca0f0b1c326fddfcb.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.61,1.62],"answerText":"1.62","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.62 (1.61 - 1.62)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1a/1a03a1340ef3a57c6e67.png\" /></div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A spur gear has 30 teeth and rotates at 300 rpm. The module of the gear is 2 mm. The pitch line velocity of the gear is ______ m/s. [Correct upto three decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.92,0.98],"answerText":"0.943","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.943 (0.920 - 0.980)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e9/e9f0a225ec3dc647c4a1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A cast iron block is machined by a horizontal slab milling cutter with a depth of cut of 4 mm, cutter diameter of 100 mm and has 6 straight teeth along its periphery. The machining is performed at a feed per tooth of 0.2 mm and at a rotational speed of 180 rpm, The mean un-cut chip thickness is ______ μm. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[38,40.2],"answerText":"39.19","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>39.19 (38.00 - 40.20)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e6a848491552b6d883e9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Two pieces of wood of section 40 mm × 40 mm are joined together along a plane inclined at 45° to the axis as shown in the figure. If the strength of the joint is 11 MPa in tension and 6 MPa in shear. The maximum axial load that the member can sustain is ______ kN. [Correct upto one decimal place]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/42fdf5b60deef9652e83.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[19.2,19.2],"answerText":"19.2","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>19.2 (19.2 - 19.2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/198610ab8b61986a023f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A capillary rise of 3 cm is observed between two vertical parallel plates having a gap of 1 mm, when dipped in a liquid (ρ = 1100 kg/m<sup>3</sup>, σ = 0.75 N/m). The contact angle of the meniscus surface with the plate is ____ degrees. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[77.4,77.8],"answerText":"77.54","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>77.54 (77.40 - 77.80)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/de/de82ca2c465efb4c0b4c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":32,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The production quantity (in thousand tons) for last four years is as follows: 20, 24, 22, 21. Using the exponential smoothing method (α = 0.3), the forecasted quantity for this year is _______ tons. [Round off to the nearest integer]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[21100,21900],"answerText":"21308","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>21308 (21100 - 21900)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5f016d9fa22a18b225a8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following surface treatment methods is/are used to improve the fatigue life of a component?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Shot peening"},{"key":"B","html":"Carburizing"},{"key":"C","html":"Nitriding"},{"key":"D","html":"Polishing"}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c, d)<br />\nDuring machining operations, small scratches and grooves are invariably introduced into the<br />\nworkpiece surface by cutting tool action. These surface markings can limit the fatigue life. It has<br />\nbeen observed that improving the surface finish by polishing will enhance fatigue Life significantly.<br />\nOne of the most effective methods of increasing fatigue. performance is by imposing residual<br />\ncompressive stresses. within a thin outer surface Layer. Residual Compressive Stresses are<br />\ncommonly introduced into ductile metals mechanically. by localized plastic deformation by a<br />\nprocess termed shot peening.<br />\nCase hardening is a technique by which both surface hardness. fatigue Life are enhanced for steel<br />\nalloys. This is accomplished by a carburizing or nitriding process.</p>"},{"n":34,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following statements is/are incorrect regarding natural convection?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"In turbulent flow over a heated vertical plate, the coefficient of heat transfer is independent of the characteristic length."},{"key":"B","html":"The characteristic length in case of a vertical cylinder is the diameter of the cylinder."},{"key":"C","html":"The ratio of buoyancy force to the viscous force is known as Rayleigh number."},{"key":"D","html":"The nusselt number is a function of a Grashof number and Prandtl number."}],"answer":["B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d793477e02b8fc0f5aa1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":35,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Let <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/a6/a644301d68fb52532ccd.png\" /> and c be the positively oriented closed curve given by x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 1, z = 0. If <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/58/583843a1fb8a92fa1994.png\" /> then the value of a is _____.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-1,-1],"answerText":"-1","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-1 (-1 - -1)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c8a48d1285719260787f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A ball is dropped on an inclined plane and after impact it is observed to move horizontally as shown in the figure. If the inclination of the plane is 30°, then the coefficient of restitution is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/232e0a39be329693d14a.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3e/3e429b5d3db6120abc67.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4b/4ba6aa42cb3ab5641db6.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/78c7dbd2939d96f73f19.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a3/a3b52849403fc02f00a6.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ac08d7ab7963a04141ca.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fc62cd8f9ca615f22a3c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A taper plug gauge is measured using the roller method as shown in the figure. The measurement over the rollers when the gauge is placed directly on the base is 68.37 mm and when the gauge is placed on a 75 mm gauge block is 72.40 mm.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e0/e0bb7146cd1acc510e5c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The rate of taper of the gauge is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3.077"},{"key":"B","html":"0.0537"},{"key":"C","html":"0.0268"},{"key":"D","html":"1.535"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4e30ce1a86358d4b3f3e.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/66/669a8eb75e80d76e255a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":38,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The available energy associated with 5.4 kg of wet steam at 100 kPa and dryness fraction 0.85 is to be determined. The dead state is at 27°C and 1 bar.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5e663b16014f3d29701.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The available energy is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"6.73 MJ"},{"key":"B","html":"63.7 kJ"},{"key":"C","html":"6.67 kJ"},{"key":"D","html":"73.6 MJ"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/08/088eb73ac8d4ef66c6cd.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Water flows over a flat plate at a free steam velocity of 0.15 m/s. There is no pressure gradient and the laminar boundary layer thickness at a given location is 5 mm. The velocity profile inside the boundary layer is given by <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/42/4213b477a8ed9acfcaf6.png\" />The local skin friction coefficient is<br />\n[Take, μ = 1.02 g/ms and ρ = 1 g/cm<sup>3</sup>]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4.27 × 10<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"3.52 × 10<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"2.31 × 10<sup>–3</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"1.93 × 10<sup>–3</sup>"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/33/33229455fbf6235afc71.png\" /></div>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Match <strong>List-I</strong> (Casting Processes) with <strong>List-II</strong> (Applications) and select the correct answer using the codes given below the lists:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/95/95aff1a796a03114ecef.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"P - 4, Q - 1, R - 2, S - 3"},{"key":"B","html":"P - 4, Q - 2, R - 1, S - 3"},{"key":"C","html":"P - 3, Q - 4, R - 2, S - 1"},{"key":"D","html":"P - 2, Q - 3, R - 4, S - 1"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\n&bull; Cylinders and cylinder heads for air cooled IC engines, automobile transmission parts, cast tooth bevel gears, refrigerator valve plate, Small Crank shafts are some of the common applications of Shell moulding.<br />\n&bull; In olden day investment casting was used for artefacts, jewellery and surgical instruments.<br />\npresently it used for vanes and blades for gas turbines, Stainless steel valve bodies and impellers for turbo chargers.<br />\n&bull; The typical products made by die casting are carburettors, crank Cases, motor cycles and<br />\nmopeds parts, and other decorative items on automobiles.<br />\n&bull; True centrifugal casting is normally used for making of hollow pipes, tubes, hollow bushes etc. which are axisymmetric with a concentric hole.</p>"},{"n":41,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A straight cylindrical bar of length 4 m is fixed at both ends and is subjected to a transverse point load of 150 N at its midpoint. Due to this load, the maximum deflection in the bar is observed to be 0.5 mm. If the same bar is loaded axially, then the load at which the bar will buckle is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"150 kN"},{"key":"B","html":"120.4 kN"},{"key":"C","html":"61.7 kN"},{"key":"D","html":"246.74 kN"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/52/52b8394c3d615eea5d75.png\" /></div>"},{"n":42,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In an offset slider crank mechanism, the offset of the slider is increased while keeping all link lengths the same. The effect on the stroke length of the slider is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Remains unchanged"},{"key":"B","html":"Increases"},{"key":"C","html":"Decreases"},{"key":"D","html":"Decreases then increases"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5ecd54dd8751bf8f9014.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A cold storage plant is required to store 15 tonnes of a dairy product. The storage temperature required is –10°C; while the product is supplied at 30°C. The cooling process is completed in 5 hours. The actual COP of the refrigeration system is 50% of the carnot COP. The power capacity<br />\nrequired to run the plant is<br />\n[Use the following data for dairy product: Specific heat above freezing point = 3 kJ/kg°C; Specific heat below freezing point = 1.5 kJ/kg°C; Freezing point = –2°C; Latent heat = 250 kJ/kg]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"45.37 kW"},{"key":"B","html":"90.74 kW"},{"key":"C","html":"0.318 kW"},{"key":"D","html":"70.45 kW"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f7/f7ee914faafd375342d8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A bolted joint consists of four identical bolts A, B, C and D as shown in the figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9ba8bc205119023b157d.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The bolts subjected to maximum shear stress, is/are</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A only"},{"key":"B","html":"B and D only"},{"key":"C","html":"A, B and D"},{"key":"D","html":"A, B, C and D"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/692ab4b3f256a94c7599.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A company uses EOQ model for inventory control. The total annual inventory cost to the company is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/64/644fb6eebbb13a6c157d.png\" /> The optimal lot size purchased by the company is 2000 units. The unit cost of the product is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/af/af2530665e6192868f64.png\" /> The percentage of carrying charges per unit of the average inventory per month is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"5.5%"},{"key":"B","html":"11%"},{"key":"C","html":"66%"},{"key":"D","html":"22%"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/da/da5869fab3489bedd3f6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A four-cylinder four-stroke engine during a test have cylinder bore 15 cm, stroke 20 cm, speed 400 rpm, brake consisting a dead load of 79 kg on one end of belt and the other end is attached to a spring balance reading 4 kg, the mean diameter of friction brake 1.2, area of indicator<br />\ndiagram 3 cm<sup>2</sup>, length of indicator diagram 6 cm and the indicator spring rating is 0.09 cm/bar. The mechanical efficiency of engine is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"35.31%"},{"key":"B","html":"74.39%"},{"key":"C","html":"37.19%"},{"key":"D","html":"70.63%"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/89/8957030518e4eba990f7.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3b/3be6c473e617c2db5aef.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e9/e955e1a28ffa4951902b.png\" /> with y(0) = 1, then y(3) = ____.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.03,0.05],"answerText":"0.04","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.04 (0.03 - 0.05)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e3c522d0bf184504921.png\" /></div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b8dbfbc15ebb545d5a7e.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"sin(2<em>u</em>)"},{"key":"B","html":"–sin(2<em>u</em>)"},{"key":"C","html":"cos(2<em>u</em>)"},{"key":"D","html":"tan(2<em>u</em>)"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5c/5ca518d900ee62ef7d70.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In a double pipe heat exchanger, hot water flows at a rate of 2.5 kg/s and is cooled from 85°C to 45°C. Simultaneously cooling water flows at a rate of 5 kg/s and enters the heat exchanged at 30°C. The overall heat transfer coefficient remains constant at 2100 W/m<sup>2</sup>k. The specific heat<br />\ncapacity of water is 4180 J/kg/k. The heat transfer area required is ______ m<sup>2</sup>. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[8.31,8.61],"answerText":"8.43","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>8.43 (8.31 - 8.61)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8dc3db7ff5458f2cc2e7.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fb/fb78585c5ac6408bfc7a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An 15 m long horizontal cantilever beam ABC is built-in at A and Supported at C, by a rigid prop as shown in the figure. Segment AB and BC carries a uniformly distributed loads of 300 N/m and 600 N/m respectively. The load taken by the prop at C is ______ kN. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/747990896b5c5410c51d.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.79,2.85],"answerText":"2.82","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.82 (2.79 - 2.85)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5a/5a0cb0beb254b6209b8c.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5c/5c5bfa870dc80ae490c2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A simple pendulum of length l has a linear spring of stiffness k attached to the bob of mass m as shown in the figure. When the system is taken from Earth to Moon, the percentage change in its natural frequency is ________%. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/95/955432df3126c773cec2.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-23.9,-23.1],"answerText":"-23.36","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-23.36 (-23.90 - -23.10)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e7/e70c022d076a59b8b5ed.png\" /></div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A closed tank of height 5 m and cross-section 2 m × 2 m contains a liquid of specific gravity 1.12. A rectangular vertical gate of height 2 m and width 2 m is provided at the bottom of the tank as shown in the figure. The distance of the centre of pressure of the net hydrostatic force acting on the gate from ground is ________ mm. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f616d57684ba06497824.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1210,1220],"answerText":"1214.95","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1214.95 (1210 - 1220)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0f/0f7a3649a8c600d0358a.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ee/ee9dae4e8c55b166eb62.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The demand for a product over seven years is given below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1fc0463bf5b81edf3985.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The forecasted-demand for the year 2027 using linear forecasting method will be ______. (Round off to the nearest integer)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[137,140],"answerText":"138","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>138 (137 - 140)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2f/2f350c1ae8f821f0eb05.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A 12 cm diameter plate is rotated in water and a 30 cm diameter plate in air under dynamically and kinematically similar conditions. If the torque required for the plate rotating in water is 3.73 kN-m, then the torque required for the plate rotating in air is ______ N-m. (Correct upto one decimal place)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7a/7a24bf0dfa578705a6b1.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[24.8,25.7],"answerText":"25.2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>25.2 (24.8 - 25.7)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9a/9a8052831f39c28569d9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A composite tie bar of length 1.2 m hanging vertically consists of a steel rod of 20 mm diameter encased in a brass tube of 20 mm internal diameter and 30 mm external diameter. The bar is rigidly fixed at the top end. The bar is suddenly loaded by a weight of 15 kN falling freely<br />\nthrough a height of 4 mm. The total extension of the bar is _____ mm. (Round off to three decimal places)<br />\n[Take, <em>E</em><sub>steel</sub> = 200 GPa; <em>E</em><sub>brass</sub> = 96 GPa]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.371,1.401],"answerText":"1.389","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.389 (1.371 - 1.401)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/56839da6f6d3866a590e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Superheated steam enters a turbine at 17 bar and 230°C and expands to 3.5 bar, where the steam is found to be 2.5% wet. The isentropic efficiency of the turbine is ________ %. (Correct upto three decimal places)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f9/f9c9c824c7e310fff2c6.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[63.41,63.49],"answerText":"63.445","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>63.445 (63.410 - 63.490)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ab/ab59852fbda61d4812cc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A cutter tip is initially at x = 2 mm, y = 2 mm. On the xy table of a NC machine, tool is to move finally to x = 62 mm, y = 2 mm. The pitch of the NC drive lead screw having double start is 1 mm. If the backlash between the lead screw and the nut is 2.7°, then the total backlash of the table on moving from initial to final point is _______ mm (Correct upto three decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.22,0.23],"answerText":"0.225","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.225 (0.220 - 0.230)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/3728a256cebd6a1f8b0f.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/13/139f0ca9a8edacad90fe.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A single slider crank mechanism has stroke length of 400 mm, mass of rotating parts is 40 kg at crank radius and mass of reciprocating parts is 51 kg. If all the revolving parts and two-third of the reciprocating parts are to be balanced, then the balancing mass required at 320 mm radius is<br />\n______ kg. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[45,47],"answerText":"46.25","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>46.25 (45.00 -47.00)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5c/5c2e5052504e379070fc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A well insulated rigid tank contains 7 kg of a saturated liquid-vapour mixture at 150 kPa. Initially 80% of the mass is in vapour phase. Heat is supplied to the content through an electrical resistance heater until 12% of the mass remains in liquid state. The entropy change of the contents during the process is _____ kJ/K. (Round off to two decimal places)<br />\nInitial state : <em>s<sub>f</sub></em> = 0.001 kJ/kgK; <em>s<sub>fg</sub></em> = 6.43 kJ/kgK<br />\nFinal state : <em>s<sub>f</sub></em> = 0.0015 kJ/kgK; <em>s<sub>fg</sub></em> = 6.36 kJ/kgK</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3.15,3.19],"answerText":"3.17","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3.17 (3.15 - 3.19)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6e/6e11221ac9aefe787c39.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A composite wall consists of two slabs <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> in parallel, having unit length normal to the plane of paper as shown in the figure. The total rate of heat transfer through composite wall is 6 kW. The thermal conductivities of slab <em>A</em> and slab <em>B</em> are 12 W/mK and 3 W/mK, respectively.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/96/968631485210352188c2.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>If thermal resistance of interference between slabs <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> is 0.1 K/W, then the rate of heat transfer through slab <em>A</em> is ______ kW. [Correct upto one decimal place]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4.2,4.8],"answerText":"4.5","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4.5 (4.2 - 4.8)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e4/e46d62bfd8cb7886d53b.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a4/a487abc38baa3cce7ca9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":61,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following processes is/are not used for tube making?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Extrusion"},{"key":"B","html":"Swaging"},{"key":"C","html":"Tube drawing"},{"key":"D","html":"Roll piercing"}],"answer":["B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, c)<br />\nTo obtain seamless tubes, extrusion can be used. It is also possible to obtain seamless tubes by a<br />\nvariation of rolling called roll piercing. Here, the billet or round stock is rolled between two rolls,<br />\nboth of them rotating in same direction with their axes at an angle of 4.5 to 6.5&deg;.<br />\nTube drawing and swaging are techniques of reducing or shaping the cross-section of tubes. In<br />\ntube drawing mandrel in required while tubes can be swaged with or without the mandrels.</p>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The velocity field in a fluid is given as</p>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ed/ed1fad050d559d36fb0d.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The flow is incompressible"},{"key":"B","html":"The flow is irrotational"},{"key":"C","html":"The convective acceleration experienced by a fluid particle is zero at (<em>x</em> = 0, <em>y</em> = 0)"},{"key":"D","html":"The temporal acceleration experienced by a fluid particle is zero at (<em>x</em> = 1, y = 1)"}],"answer":["A","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b3/b3e86de334686fde5854.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b2/b2e01bf3816409255b32.png\" /></div>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The daily consumption of electric power (in millions of kW-hours) is a Random variable having the <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/08/082ff348c74c380ae874.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>If the total production each day is 12 million kW-hours, the probability that there is power cut (shortage) on any given day is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3 <em>e</em><sup>–4</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"4 <em>e</em><sup>–4</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"5 <em>e</em><sup>–4</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"6 <em>e</em><sup>–4</sup>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/098e354633a6b56f6dc7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The determinant of the given matrix is ____________.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/12/1267f3ce630f2192d1f0.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[12,12],"answerText":"12","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>12 (12 - 12)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b07e9ff6f1d6a2ac3f21.png\" /></div>"},{"n":65,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the first order initial value problem y′ = y + 2x – x<sup>2</sup>, y(0) = 1, 0 ≤ x < ∞ with exact solution y(x) = x<sup>2</sup> + ex. For x = 0.2, the percentage difference between the exact solution and the solution obtained using a single iteration of the second-order Runge-Kutta method with stepsize<br />\nh = 0.2 is _____%. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.5,0.59],"answerText":"0.54","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.54 (0.50 - 0.59)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b6/b6fecda2d9b60c006d9d.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":33,"MSQ":5,"NAT":27},"withoutKey":0}};
